WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:04.290
Single-player games are meant to be played…well,
alone.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.290
That's the point.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:09.440
But when it comes to horror games, particularly
survival horror, you may want some company

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.929
before you dive head-on into an unknown environment.

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:18.290
Even if you're a horror game veteran, we don't
recommend playing any of these games by yourself.

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:19.290
Outlast

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:23.330
A horror game in which a journalist investigates
a freaked-out psychiatric hospital may sound

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.690
clichéd, but Outlast is anything but.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:30.650
The Amnesia-inspired survival horror game
arrived in 2013, marking the first release

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.260
by the Canadian indie developer Red Barrels.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:38.140
Aside from the environment being unnerving,
Outlast's story is intriguing enough to keep

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.480
players immersed.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.300
But what really hooks gamers are the mechanics.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.560
There's an indescribable dizzying effect to
the game that somehow makes it all the more

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.450
vivid, and the first-person perspective heightens
the entire experience.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.570
We'd wager that more people paused the game
not because they needed to get up and stretch,

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.649
but because the game just got too scary.

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:00.850
Outlast is unique among horror games.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:05.979
As a reporter, you're armed only with a camera,
and unless you're using it as a blunt instrument,

00:01:05.979 --> 00:01:08.789
cameras are notoriously sucky weapons.

00:01:08.789 --> 00:01:13.380
Even worse, its night vision mode is all you
have to lighten up the hospital.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:19.090
You don't have a gun, a crowbar, or a kickass
limb-rending chainsaw to defend yourself.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:21.909
If you see someone charging you, run.

00:01:21.909 --> 00:01:23.170
That's your only move.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:27.799
And given how scary this game is, you'll probably
be running before you realize you triggered

00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:29.799
your fight-or-flight response.

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:33.789
Even if you have a few people with you, playing
the game in broad daylight, with the sound

00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:37.789
barely loud enough to hear, you still might
not be able to finish.

00:01:37.789 --> 00:01:39.710
Resident Evil 4

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:43.549
The most well-known horror franchise is probably
Resident Evil.

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:47.429
That's due, at least in part, to how long
it's been around, as well as the enormously

00:01:47.429 --> 00:01:49.939
successful movie franchise it spawned.

00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:54.869
In fact, it's the only video game film series
that's ended on its own terms.

00:01:54.869 --> 00:01:59.399
While the games have become much more action-oriented
and less about survival horror, they still

00:01:59.399 --> 00:02:01.240
have their frightening moments.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:04.709
The best is undoubtedly Resident Evil 4.

00:02:04.709 --> 00:02:08.629
Even if you don't find the game as scary as
other installments, there's no doubt it keeps

00:02:08.629 --> 00:02:10.569
you at the edge of your seat.

00:02:10.569 --> 00:02:14.819
Resident Evil 4 has plenty of creepy moments
for which you don’t want to be alone — in-game

00:02:14.819 --> 00:02:16.069
or otherwise.

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:19.819
The setting creates suspense and terror during
moments where you're not even progressing

00:02:19.819 --> 00:02:21.150
through the story.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:25.700
Have you walked into a place and said to yourself,
"This seems creepy?”

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.870
That's exactly what Resident Evil 4 is like,
and that's what makes it terrifying.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:32.590
Just exploring is scary enough.

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:34.060
Silent Hill 2

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:38.920
It might be one of the greatest stories in
gaming history — and one of the scariest.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.349
You may play every horror game out there without
being frightened, then play Silent Hill 2

00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:46.340
and feel something unlike anything you've
experienced.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:51.410
On the surface, Silent Hill 2 feels like Resident
Evil in many ways, but fundamentally, the

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.579
game makes you work hard to see its ending.

00:02:53.579 --> 00:02:57.819
Rather than granting players the freedom to
wander around and do whatever they please,

00:02:57.819 --> 00:03:02.439
Silent Hill 2 is crafted to deliver a genre-defining
horror experience.

00:03:02.439 --> 00:03:04.560
Alien: Isolation

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.959
The original Alien movies are acknowledged
as classics — and rightfully so.

00:03:08.959 --> 00:03:13.290
But its status as a beloved movie franchise
means that developer Creative Assembly had

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:18.260
their work cut out for them when Sega commissioned
the studio to create a new Alien video game.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:23.370
Isolation takes place 15 years after the events
of the first Alien film, centering on Ellen

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:28.189
Ripley's daughter, Amanda Ripley, as she investigates
her mother's disappearance.

00:03:28.189 --> 00:03:31.890
Unlike most survival horror games, which are
meant to frighten you as much as possible

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:37.830
with suspense and jump scares, Alien: Isolation
focuses heavily on stealth, amplifying the

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:40.170
suspense factor organically.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.550
You don't want the alien to find you.

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:43.810
At all.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:48.189
If you really want to have the ultimate horror
experience, play Isolation with a virtual

00:03:48.189 --> 00:03:49.720
reality device.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:53.939
Compounded with the stealth gameplay, it just
might be a heart-stopping experience.

00:03:53.939 --> 00:03:55.150
F.E.A.R.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:58.670
Most survival horror games take place in a
secluded environment in which the player is

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.319
alone in an abandoned area or building.

00:04:01.319 --> 00:04:02.319
F.E.A.R.

00:04:02.319 --> 00:04:03.579
is a little bit different.

00:04:03.579 --> 00:04:08.730
The developers at Monolith Productions successfully
managed to combine the best elements of Japanese

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:12.829
horror genre and first-person shooters, and
they did so while also providing a unique

00:04:12.829 --> 00:04:13.999
story.

00:04:13.999 --> 00:04:18.140
Throughout the series, players take control
of numerous protagonists, set across different

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:19.330
time periods.

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:24.630
But the villain is always the supernatural
being Alma Wade, first depicted as an eight-year-old

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.060
girl, and later an adult woman.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:31.880
In the first game, it's unclear if Alma is,
in fact, real, at all — or if she is able

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:36.630
to manifest herself into the consciousness
of her victims...like some sort of adorable

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:37.750
Freddy Krueger.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:42.060
The game has a pretty convoluted story arc,
which involves everything from supernatural

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:46.760
phenomena, government conspiracies, and even
a character who closely resembles the girl

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.440
from The Ring thrown in for good measure.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.611
In the first installment, players take control
of the Point Man, the leader of the First

00:04:53.611 --> 00:04:56.300
Encounter Assault Recon, or F.E.A.R.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.300
team.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:01.330
Along with members of Delta Force, they're
ordered to eliminate someone named Paxton

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:05.310
Fettel, who is psychically controlling a group
of super-soldiers.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:09.540
The game's director once said he wanted players
to feel like they're the hero in an action

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:10.540
movie.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:12.120
That's precisely what playing F.E.A.R.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:18.230
feels like, albeit augmented with the actual
fear of encountering creepy little Alma.

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:19.230
SOMA

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:23.220
Have you ever seen a movie that wasn't particularly
scary, at least not in the traditional sense

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:27.260
of the word, but was instead disturbing on
a fundamental level?

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.760
That's what SOMA's like.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.370
But a video game.

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:35.150
The developers at Frictional Games combined
the best gameplay aspects from their Amnesia

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:40.650
series, which itself might be one of the most
terrifying around, and tweaked them for SOMA.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:43.120
There's nothing conventional about this game.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:47.860
There's no combat, jump scares are limited,
and the monsters aren't all that frightening.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:51.950
The studio's creative director, Thomas Grip,
said that spooking and surprising players

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:54.590
wasn't what the game was supposed to be anyway.

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:55.590
He said,

00:05:55.590 --> 00:06:01.510
"The fact of the matter is that SOMA, just
like Amnesia, is very much a horror game.

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:05.800
It's just that it is presented in a different
manner, using slower build-up and more focus

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.450
on the psychological aspects."

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:10.880
In that regard, he's right.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:15.740
SOMA messes with you psychologically, screwing
with your mind, making the most obscure elements

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.980
feel eerier than anything else.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:23.110
Play this one with a friend, just so you can
stay a little more sane.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:24.740
The Evil Within

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:30.140
In the late 2000s, developers seemed to be
focusing more on action than horror, and Resident

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:35.800
Evil creator Shinji Mikami strived to change
that with his new horror game, The Evil Within.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:36.910
He told IGN,

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:40.610
"Survival horror as a genre is becoming all
action now.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:42.580
That is the biggest motivation for me.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:48.360
…Having the player pick up the controller
and being genuinely able to say, 'Wow, I haven't

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:52.560
played a game this scary in ages!,' that is
what we are after."

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:57.470
When Mikami directs a new survival horror
game, you know it's going to be scary — and

00:06:57.470 --> 00:07:00.260
The Evil Within is downright terrifying.

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:04.670
If you're already a fan of the horror genre
then you may be a veteran.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:07.300
As such, you might not need someone to play
with.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:11.000
But there's no denying its effectiveness,
and having a buddy on the couch might make

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.370
you less likely to pee your pants.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:18.080
The survival horror elements, combined with
the scarcity of resources, make The Evil Within

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.500
even scarier.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:23.020
It's not the jump scares that get you, it's
realizing that you're out of ammo and have

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:26.800
nowhere to go, with enemies coming at you
from all directions.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.840
Five Nights at Freddy's 4

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:33.000
The first installment in the Five Nights at
Freddy's series was scary in its own way,

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.810
while the second and third games were more
on the silly side.

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:41.050
Five Nights at Freddy's 4, however, is undoubtedly
the scariest in the whole series.

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:45.250
Switching from a security office setting to
a child's bedroom instantly heightens the

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:46.830
suspense and fear.

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:51.150
The game triggers memories for people who
were once afraid of the dark, or afraid that

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:55.730
a monster was in their closet or under their
bed...or was the bed.

00:07:55.730 --> 00:08:00.270
Imagine all of those terrifying fears come
true — and the only item you can defend

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:02.830
yourself with is a dinky flashlight.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:06.530
That's Five Nights at Freddy's 4, and it's
absolutely terrifying.

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:07.530
Fatal Frame

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:12.280
The Fatal Frame series is one of the longest-running
horror game franchises.

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:16.390
But the first game, released in 2001, is perhaps
the scariest.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:21.330
If you're a fan of the Silent Hill series,
you're going to love Fatal Frame, or Project

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.700
Zero, as it was titled in Europe.

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:29.390
Fatal Frame takes place in the haunted Himuro
Mansion in Japan, unfolding across multiple

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:33.920
chapters, and it's the player's job to uncover
the mansion's secrets and determine what happened

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:34.920
to its inhabitants.

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:39.050
It's not only about surviving, or about advancing
to the next level.

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:44.180
It's also about the psychological impact the
game will have on you once you're done playing.

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:48.420
That's the beauty of Fatal Frame; it's not
a game that throws unnecessary jump scares

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.590
at you, because it doesn't have to.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.630
It's all about the suspense.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:56.650
If you have trouble sleeping or being home
alone at night after watching a really scary

00:08:56.650 --> 00:09:01.710
horror movie, that's exactly the feeling you'll
have if you play Fatal Frame alone.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.620
Consider yourself warned.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:07.580
Make sure you phone a friend to share the
terror.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:08.840
Daylight

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:13.680
Writer Jessica Chobot invented a unique story
with a classic setting with Daylight.

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:18.770
Players are tasked with uncovering the secrets
of a hospital by discovering remnants, acquiring

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:24.340
sigils, and bringing them to the Seal of Shadows,
all so they can advance through the game and

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:26.340
eventually escape the forsaken building.

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:31.230
Though the story isn't anything special, what
makes Daylight a truly terrifying game is

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:36.660
rooted deep down in its core — it's survival
horror in the truest sense of the term.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:41.390
Armed with only glow sticks, flares, and a
cellphone, players avoid shadow people while

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.190
searching for a way out.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:47.280
And when players are confronted, the only
thing they can do is either use a flare or

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:48.830
just run.

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:53.560
Unlike other survival horror games, Daylight's
environment is randomly generated.

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:56.620
Every time you play, it's different from the
last time.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:10:01.920
Unfortunately, the developer, Zombie Studios,
shuttered the following year, all but eliminating

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:03.930
any chance for a sequel.

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:05.279
Thanks for watching!

00:10:05.279 --> 00:10:07.910
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:09.920
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

